WEBVTT

00:08.190 --> 00:10.190
Are you recording?

00:10.190 --> 00:11.820
Can I talk?

00:12.360 --> 00:14.240
Kan, you say something.

00:14.450 --> 00:16.950
Hey there! It's Kanshi.

00:16.950 --> 00:18.620
It's Nico.

00:18.620 --> 00:22.040
And so, what are we doing today, Nico?

00:22.040 --> 00:25.210
Wait, I'm going to say it?
Kan, you say it.

00:26.290 --> 00:29.800
We'll be singing an original song
that we made.

00:29.960 --> 00:31.880
Yay!

00:32.210 --> 00:38.760
The sun is smiling in the sky.
We can, can, smile, smile! So happy!

00:38.760 --> 00:46.020
[PARENT ALERT] OUR ROOMMATE BURST IN
WHILE WE WERE FILMING LOLOL

00:39.140 --> 00:42.270
<i>Shut up! What the hell
are you guys doing at this hour?</i>

02:18.740 --> 02:20.240
You're uploading videos?

02:19.070 --> 02:22.990
KAN AND NICO'S CHANNEL

02:20.240 --> 02:23.370
Yeah! I heard you can easily make money
if you become a YouTuber.

02:23.370 --> 02:24.790
I heard it's easy!

02:24.790 --> 02:26.620
Don't underestimate YouTubers!

02:26.620 --> 02:31.130
It's not a world that you two idiots can
casually take on and get famous.

02:31.500 --> 02:33.540
There're way too many youngsters

02:33.540 --> 02:36.260
who imitate other YouTubers,
get bored of it, and then quit.

02:36.260 --> 02:38.760
But the thing is, Morihito...

02:38.920 --> 02:41.680
I heard you can make money
just by having fun.

02:42.680 --> 02:45.180
Who the hell
is spreading such false lies?

02:45.470 --> 02:47.770
Sergeant Punch at Hyoutan Park.

02:47.770 --> 02:49.810
I don't know who that is,
but he sounds dumb!

02:50.350 --> 02:54.520
Geez, I was wondering what you guys
were doing lately every night.

02:54.520 --> 02:57.900
Oh well, so what kind of videos
have you been making?

02:58.320 --> 03:02.070
Kan and Nico's Channel.
Sounds like Kan and Aki's Channel.

03:02.740 --> 03:04.700
Your subscriber count is so low!

03:04.700 --> 03:06.740
This reeks of imitation.

03:06.740 --> 03:09.500
And the thumbnails
don't even pull me in.

03:10.660 --> 03:12.040
LET'S PLAY

03:12.040 --> 03:16.880
<i>Oh come on!
This enemy really pisses me off!</i>

03:12.040 --> 03:16.880
[LET'S PLAY] KANSHI PLAYS SMASH KANGAROO

03:16.880 --> 03:18.760
Ugh, this is horrible.

03:18.050 --> 03:22.180
<i>This game isn't balanced at all!
I should call support and complain.</i>

03:18.760 --> 03:22.180
It's just a video of Kanshi placing
a camera behind him while playing a game.

03:22.680 --> 03:26.680
He's just being salty and mumbling
negativity. How annoying.

03:26.810 --> 03:28.180
I TRIED DANCING

03:28.180 --> 03:31.270
<i>Rain, rain, go away.
Come again another day.</i>

03:28.180 --> 03:34.440
[I TRIED DANCING] REALLY HARD TO "RAIN, RAIN, GO AWAY"

03:31.270 --> 03:34.150
A children's song?
Dance to a song that's popular!

03:34.980 --> 03:39.570
She's being so awkward while dancing.
I can't, this is too cringey.

03:39.690 --> 03:41.070
UNBOXING

03:41.070 --> 03:51.830
[UNBOXING] WE BOUGHT A HAIR DRYER!

03:44.320 --> 03:45.990
<i>Do you need scissors?</i>

03:45.990 --> 03:48.240
<i>Hmm, just give me a second.</i>

03:49.700 --> 03:50.700
<i>I can't get it.</i>

03:50.700 --> 03:51.830
For the love of god, edit!

03:52.080 --> 03:54.460
What the hell is this? It's all crap!

03:54.710 --> 03:56.750
Like home videos with no self-control.

03:56.750 --> 03:58.840
But he said we can easily make money.

03:58.840 --> 04:01.220
Forget about
Sergeant Punch's mutterings.

04:01.510 --> 04:06.300
Listen. It's really difficult to make videos
that will remain in peoples' hearts.

04:06.550 --> 04:08.600
Plus, if you want advertising revenue,

04:06.550 --> 04:12.850
KAN AND NICO ARE MINORS,
SO IT'S A PARENT'S ACCOUNT

04:08.600 --> 04:12.850
you need a considerable
amount of views and subscribers.

04:12.850 --> 04:16.860
15 VIEWS

04:13.480 --> 04:16.110
What's this "15 views"?

04:16.360 --> 04:18.690
Is it you guys just replaying
your own video?

04:18.690 --> 04:21.110
No, people have left comments, too.

04:21.110 --> 04:23.110
KANSHI'S VOICE SOUNDS LIKE A VOICE ACTOR'S

04:21.690 --> 04:23.110
These are definitely your friends.

04:23.110 --> 04:25.200
NICO, I WATCHED IT

04:23.400 --> 04:25.200
That's Kuku and Kara.

04:25.450 --> 04:28.370
Dang it, there're only three comments
and we already got a flamer.

04:25.450 --> 04:28.370
MY CLASSMATE STARTED POSTING VIDEOS,
SO I CHECKED IT OUT. BUT WHAT THE HELL
IS THIS TRASH? YOU'RE JUST STEALING THE FORMAT
OF POPULAR VIDEOS. HAVE YOU HEARD OF EDITING?
WHO THE HELL IS WATCHING THESE VIDEOS?
WELL I GUESS I WATCHED IT LULZ

04:28.370 --> 04:30.040
That's probably Arashi Komeran.

04:30.040 --> 04:31.870
Flaming is not our friend!

04:32.200 --> 04:36.960
Like Komeran wrote,
your channel has no uniqueness.

04:36.960 --> 04:39.130
You're validating him?

04:39.460 --> 04:42.880
Your videos are all over the place
and don't have any concept.

04:43.220 --> 04:46.640
You should make videos that enhance
each of your distinct characteristics.

04:47.180 --> 04:50.260
Even if you say that, we don't have
any distinct characteristics.

04:50.260 --> 04:52.060
We're just two dummies!

04:52.060 --> 04:55.480
It's not like we can upload videos
about our magic and mystic powers...

04:55.480 --> 04:56.770
Of course not!

04:57.900 --> 05:02.070
If you're serious about this,
I might have someone who you can talk to.

05:05.450 --> 05:09.200
This is Keigo Magami,
our class's loser hipster guy.

05:09.200 --> 05:11.740
Maybe don't call him a loser
when he's right there?

05:11.740 --> 05:14.040
Wait, when did you two
become friends?

05:14.370 --> 05:18.580
We're not friends or anything,
but we've started talking.

05:18.960 --> 05:20.880
Uploading videos, huh?

05:20.880 --> 05:23.300
Well, I indeed do that, in a sense.

05:23.960 --> 05:28.760
Even if you watch my videos,
I don't think you'll really get them.

05:29.600 --> 05:34.140
There's a range to my content,
but I think introducing is the main one?

05:34.350 --> 05:38.060
I buy all kinds of gadgets and items
that catch my eye.

05:38.060 --> 05:40.230
I also do movie reviews

05:40.520 --> 05:45.360
and introduce new bands because
you've probably never heard about them.

05:45.360 --> 05:47.320
I mean, they're just not well-known.

05:47.450 --> 05:49.320
I'm always chasing those indie artists.

05:49.700 --> 05:52.490
I'm seriously such a weird guy. Yeah.

05:53.660 --> 05:55.290
Are you guys uploading something, too?

05:55.290 --> 05:56.460
Yeah, about that...

05:56.460 --> 05:59.080
But I don't know
if you can use me as a reference,

05:59.080 --> 06:01.090
since I just learned everything on my own.

06:01.380 --> 06:05.970
I'm just relying on my senses so I don't have
any real structure or anything like that.

06:06.090 --> 06:09.720
I just do what I want and probably
end up making weird videos.

06:11.760 --> 06:14.010
Yeah, I'm probably kinda weird.

06:14.010 --> 06:16.180
Oh my god,
what are you going on about?

06:16.180 --> 06:17.770
Hurry up and show us the video!

06:18.390 --> 06:20.400
You're getting up in my space.

06:20.900 --> 06:22.730
I can't deal with someone like you.

06:22.730 --> 06:25.280
These guys are polar opposites.

06:25.780 --> 06:31.030
KEIGO MAGAMI ~INVISIBLE RAINBOW~
SUBSCRIBERS: 83 PEOPLE
[USED BOOK] THE RARE BOOK THAT MAGAMI GOT
102 VIEWS

06:26.280 --> 06:28.200
Here's my channel.

06:28.490 --> 06:31.030
"Keigo Magami, Invisible Rainbow."

06:31.240 --> 06:32.580
Ugh, shut up.

06:32.580 --> 06:34.620
You also don't have that many subscribers.

06:34.620 --> 06:36.290
Let's just watch one.

06:36.290 --> 06:47.670
[SERIOUSLY THE BEST] WHEN DIRECTOR MANGOSTEEN
MOGI'S NEWEST FILM WAS WAY TOO GOOD

06:37.000 --> 06:39.710
<i>What's up guys, it's Keigo.</i>

06:40.210 --> 06:42.750
<i>Today, we'll be going over
the popular romantic movie,</i>

06:43.380 --> 06:46.170
<i>"You Showed Me Something With My Eyes."
We'll be reviewing this today!</i>

06:46.170 --> 06:47.670
You what now?

06:47.920 --> 06:51.300
<i>Oh man, like seriously this was the best,
I mean the best movie!</i>

06:51.300 --> 06:55.600
<i>Starting from Act 1, to Act 2, then
all the way to Act 3, it was pretty great!</i>

06:55.600 --> 06:57.180
What was great about it?

06:57.640 --> 06:59.100
<i>So this movie was the long-awaited</i>

06:59.100 --> 07:04.730
<i>new release from the director of
"The Naughty Monk Series," Mangosteen Mogi.</i>

07:04.730 --> 07:05.940
The who and what now?

07:06.320 --> 07:09.200
<i>I was so looking forward to this movie,</i>

07:09.650 --> 07:14.950
<i>because I have a lot respect
for this director, Mangosteen Mogi.</i>

07:14.950 --> 07:18.620
<i>I mean, I also like other directors like
Don Kabashima and Skalski,</i>

07:18.620 --> 07:20.870
<i>but you probably haven't heard of them.</i>

07:20.870 --> 07:23.170
<i>Oh what? Am I the only one who likes them?</i>

07:23.170 --> 07:29.050
<i>It really grabs at my heart when
I watch things that no one else watches.</i>

07:29.050 --> 07:31.970
<i>But because of that, I don't have
many friends who I can talk to.</i>

07:32.180 --> 07:35.720
<i>That's just who I am,
and it can't be helped, right?</i>

07:35.720 --> 07:38.220
PLEASE SUBSCRIBE

07:36.560 --> 07:38.220
<i>"Invisible Rainbow."</i>

07:38.560 --> 07:41.310
<i>By the way, did you guys watch
Director Mangosteen Mogi's</i>

07:41.310 --> 07:44.810
<i>debut film, "The Imperfect Wink" yet?</i>

07:44.810 --> 07:47.780
<i>That actually has an original manga to it,</i>

07:47.780 --> 07:49.990
<i>and it's super unpopular
so you've probably never heard of it,</i>

07:49.990 --> 07:51.990
<i>but it's actually
affected my life tremendously.</i>

07:51.990 --> 07:54.570
<i>Back when I would stand out in class,
well, I still stand out now,</i>

07:54.570 --> 07:55.740
<i>it's become my emotional support
throughout the years.</i>

07:55.740 --> 07:58.080
<i>It taught me not to worry about what other
people think, and that I should just be me.</i>

07:58.080 --> 07:59.750
<i>That's what I got from that series.
Oh yeah, by the way...</i>

07:59.870 --> 08:01.370
That's enough!

08:01.370 --> 08:02.830
What the hell is this?

08:02.830 --> 08:05.250
Hurry up and tell us about that movie!

08:05.250 --> 08:09.340
You just keep talking about yourself
and only yourself, and can't stay on topic!

08:09.340 --> 08:11.220
But in the later half of the video...

08:11.220 --> 08:15.010
Just get to the subject
and end it already! It's too long!

08:15.010 --> 08:16.510
Your other videos...

08:16.720 --> 08:18.600
"Magami's Favorite Quotes."

08:19.010 --> 08:20.930
"Magami's T-Shirt Collection."

08:21.600 --> 08:23.390
"Magami's Morning Routine."

08:23.520 --> 08:25.400
None of that sounds interesting.

08:25.400 --> 08:27.400
The need for self-approval
is strong for this one.

08:27.400 --> 08:28.770
Leave me alone, will you?

08:28.770 --> 08:30.900
I'm kinda interested
in your T-shirt collection.

08:31.280 --> 08:33.450
Well, regardless of the content,

08:33.820 --> 08:39.540
Magami's videos had more professionalism
to them compared to the Kan and Nico videos.

08:40.040 --> 08:44.210
Can you only teach them
how to increase their viewership?

08:44.210 --> 08:46.920
You're a nice person,
but kind of rude, huh?

08:47.710 --> 08:51.510
<i>And so, Keigo Magami lectured them
on the important points</i>

08:51.510 --> 08:53.880
<i>of posting videos to the internet.</i>

08:54.260 --> 08:59.050
I see. Thumbnail, editing, opening,
and background music are all important.

08:59.050 --> 09:03.730
You're utilizing all these points,
but why won't your viewership increase?

09:03.730 --> 09:06.690
Uh, well... As I said,
my videos are pretty niche!

09:06.690 --> 09:08.940
And I don't intend for people
to understand them.

09:09.190 --> 09:13.440
12,000 VIEWS

09:09.690 --> 09:12.690
There's one video with a lot of views.

09:12.690 --> 09:17.450
Oh, I programmed a simple game,
and introduced it.

09:17.450 --> 09:19.530
That unexpectedly got a lot of views.

09:19.530 --> 09:20.830
Amazing!

09:20.830 --> 09:22.580
THIS IS HILARIOUS
GOT A SCREW LOOSE THERE BUDDY

09:20.830 --> 09:23.450
You're getting teased in the comments.

09:22.580 --> 09:26.330
WHAT A TRASH GAME
I ACTUALLY KNOW THE GUY WHO MADE THIS
AND HE'S DEF A LOSER HIPSTER.
HE THINKS HE'S COOL BECAUSE
HE'S DOING SOMETHING DIFFERENT

09:23.450 --> 09:26.330
It's fine! As long as people watch it, it's okay.

09:26.330 --> 09:29.080
What? Is that true?

09:29.080 --> 09:31.590
- Yeah, I'm just an idiot.
- But you're teaching us!

09:30.590 --> 09:31.590
Okay.

09:32.210 --> 09:34.340
We're gonna film a "Let's Play."

09:34.670 --> 09:36.720
I borrowed equipment from Magami.

09:36.720 --> 09:38.470
I brought some other stuff, too.

09:38.470 --> 09:40.100
Wow, thanks!

09:40.510 --> 09:42.260
It's manga!

09:42.260 --> 09:47.350
Yeah, I don't know though.
I like it, but if you read it, you might not.

09:48.060 --> 09:48.940
A movie, huh?

09:48.940 --> 09:53.860
Ohh, I only watch B movies though,
so you might not get it.

09:54.320 --> 09:57.490
This is a bad game,
so I think I'm the only one who likes it.

09:57.490 --> 09:58.860
Then don't bring it!

10:00.570 --> 10:03.910
We'll play Magami's game.

10:04.080 --> 10:05.250
The player will be Nico.

10:05.620 --> 10:07.370
I've acquired a green screen.

10:07.580 --> 10:08.870
This looks serious!

10:08.870 --> 10:11.000
He's getting serious.

10:12.340 --> 10:14.710
Just sit here and play
as you would normally.

10:14.710 --> 10:16.260
What should I do?

10:16.760 --> 10:18.010
Stay out of the shot.

10:18.340 --> 10:19.260
What?

10:20.050 --> 10:24.010
<i>With that, they filmed a video
entirely with Morihito's directions,</i>

10:24.010 --> 10:26.020
<i>and edited by Morihito.</i>

10:26.230 --> 10:28.060
I think you should put some text here.

10:28.060 --> 10:28.890
Sounds good.

10:30.230 --> 10:35.650
The meticulous, studious person paired with
the loser hipster actually make a great team, huh?

10:35.780 --> 10:38.150
[LET'S PLAY] I PLAYED MY FRIEND'S CRAP GAME

10:36.110 --> 10:37.820
<i>And then, it was uploaded!</i>

10:38.650 --> 10:41.660
The sun is smiling in the sky!

10:41.660 --> 10:46.910
We can, can, smile, smile!
Kan and Nico Channel!

10:47.540 --> 10:52.290
Hey there, hey there,
hey there folks! It's Nico!

10:52.290 --> 10:53.590
And Kanshi!

10:53.590 --> 10:56.920
Today, we'll be playing a game
that our friend made!

10:57.010 --> 10:59.430
Okay, let's get started. Hey there, go!

11:01.430 --> 11:04.680
It's a game called
"Slime Lotion Gel Amoeba."

11:02.550 --> 11:07.430
SLIME LOTION GEL AMOEBA

11:04.680 --> 11:07.430
Don't say it like, "Red Hot Chili Peppers."

11:09.140 --> 11:14.400
Let's see, in this slimy world, you lead
two grasshoppers to the goal.

11:14.400 --> 11:15.820
That's kind of a weird game.

11:16.280 --> 11:18.070
Can't you make it look a bit more cutesy?

11:18.400 --> 11:19.650
Here we go.

11:20.280 --> 11:21.910
Whoa! It's slippery!

11:21.910 --> 11:24.120
Oh no, the two grasshoppers might clash.

11:24.120 --> 11:26.580
Why do I have to watch two bugs
sumo wrestling in lotion?

11:26.870 --> 11:28.910
Wait, I don't know which is which?

11:28.910 --> 11:30.830
Why are they the same color?

11:32.170 --> 11:32.830
It died.

11:32.830 --> 11:35.210
It died?! With just that?

11:35.210 --> 11:38.880
The ground is all slippery
and the surroundings are all spikey.

11:38.880 --> 11:40.470
It's a world of madness.

11:40.970 --> 11:44.970
I got it!
If I keep somersaulting, I won't slip.

11:45.100 --> 11:47.470
What the hell is wrong
with the developer of this game?

11:47.810 --> 11:50.140
I feel like I'm in a nightmare.

11:50.140 --> 11:52.140
You're a grasshopper,
so can you jump?

11:52.140 --> 11:53.100
I can, but...

11:54.440 --> 11:56.110
It jumps too hard and dies!

11:57.020 --> 11:58.440
How many times are you dying?

11:58.440 --> 12:01.400
We haven't even advanced
since we started playing!

12:02.490 --> 12:05.370
<i>And then, this video went viral!</i>

12:02.490 --> 12:05.370
[LET'S PLAY] I PLAYED MY FRIEND'S CRAP GAME

12:06.330 --> 12:08.370
The viewership just keeps growing!

12:08.370 --> 12:10.200
And it's only been a few hours
since we uploaded it.

12:10.200 --> 12:12.410
Our follower count grew by a lot, too!

12:11.870 --> 12:13.000
THIS IS HILARIOUS.
I LOVE YOUR REACTIONS

12:12.410 --> 12:14.540
And the comments look good, too.

12:13.000 --> 12:14.540
NICO'S EXPRESSIONS ARE CUTE
KANSHI'S JAB'S ARE FUNNY

12:14.880 --> 12:16.340
We did it, Morihito!

12:16.340 --> 12:18.550
Thank you Moi, and Keigo!

12:18.960 --> 12:20.050
Yeah.

12:20.050 --> 12:23.550
[LET'S PLAY] I PLAYED MY FRIEND'S CRAP GAME

12:20.340 --> 12:23.550
Wow, I didn't think
people would love this video.

12:23.800 --> 12:27.760
The most important thing
is to utilize the performers' uniqueness.

12:27.970 --> 12:30.640
Magami's game that brought out
his strange sense.

12:31.730 --> 12:33.770
Kanshi's voice-only side jabs.

12:34.690 --> 12:35.690
And then...

12:35.940 --> 12:37.520
Nico's cuteness!

12:39.020 --> 12:42.820
If you have a weapon to use in battle,
you gotta use it to the fullest.

12:44.910 --> 12:48.740
<i>Afterwards, the Kan and Nico Channel
posted three more videos,</i>

12:45.570 --> 12:47.320
[SURPRISE] WE SURPRISED NICO
THREE TIMES IN A ROW, AND...

12:47.320 --> 12:49.370
[GACHA] A SUPER RARE FIND
IN THE PLANT AND HUMANOID SERIES...

12:48.740 --> 12:50.790
<i>which all did fairly well.</i>

12:49.370 --> 12:51.200
[COOKING] NICO BAKES SWEETS
WHILE KANSHI JABS

12:51.450 --> 12:52.660
<i>And then...</i>

12:52.790 --> 12:54.830
Hey, what are we filming next?

12:56.170 --> 12:58.290
I'm a bit busy right now.

12:58.290 --> 12:59.380
<i>They got bored with it!</i>

13:00.130 --> 13:03.550
It's the youngsters who imitated
other YouTubers and then quit!

13:14.480 --> 13:17.730
Nico, you're on duty this week, right?

13:14.480 --> 13:21.440
THE TEA CEREMONY IS A PIECE OF TEA CAKE

13:18.060 --> 13:19.980
Here's the class journal.

13:19.980 --> 13:21.980
Oh, thanks so much.

13:22.400 --> 13:24.110
<i>That's Suzuka Kiyomiya.</i>

13:24.110 --> 13:28.780
<i>Beautiful on the inside and outside,
and the daughter of an elite family.</i>

13:28.780 --> 13:31.990
<i>She's also smart and basically flawless.</i>

13:32.410 --> 13:34.710
<i>I secretly want to be just like her.</i>

13:35.500 --> 13:40.500
<i>I bet this is the type of girl that
Moi likes. Traditional and prim.</i>

13:40.710 --> 13:43.130
<i>Oh, I adore her.</i>

13:43.130 --> 13:45.970
<i>She probably has a great singing voice,
can cook well,</i>

13:45.970 --> 13:48.550
<i>and has beautiful handwriting.</i>

13:49.510 --> 13:51.010
SUZUKA KIYOMIYA

13:51.180 --> 13:53.640
<i>Kiyomiya, your writing is so messy!</i>

13:55.770 --> 13:58.850
I'm actually inept at a lot of things.

13:58.850 --> 14:00.360
That's surprising.

14:00.360 --> 14:03.400
Kiyomiya, I saw you as the type
who can do anything well.

14:03.610 --> 14:08.070
I possess the knowledge,
but I can never execute anything well.

14:08.360 --> 14:12.790
Ever since I was a child, my grandmother
put me through all kinds of lessons.

14:12.790 --> 14:15.660
But when I write poetry,
I'm told that it looks like an evil sigil.

14:15.830 --> 14:18.670
When I arrange flowers, I'm told
it looks like an insect from the demon world.

14:18.870 --> 14:20.170
When I dance the traditional dance,

14:20.170 --> 14:22.920
I'm told that I look like
a possessed marionette doll.

14:23.090 --> 14:25.670
Why is everything compared
to something devilish?

14:25.970 --> 14:28.800
I even made this bento lunch
that I have here.

14:28.800 --> 14:30.930
That chicken karaage looks delicious.

14:31.760 --> 14:33.930
This is supposed to be fried shrimp.

14:34.060 --> 14:35.770
How clumsy are you?

14:35.980 --> 14:38.810
So what you wanted to talk to me about...

14:39.140 --> 14:40.690
Please, Nico!

14:40.810 --> 14:43.070
Please make me skillful with your magic!

14:43.070 --> 14:45.650
I can give you lots of money for it!

14:45.650 --> 14:47.570
Also terrible at asking for things.

14:48.450 --> 14:52.160
So, there isn't a spell that can do
what you're looking for.

14:52.410 --> 14:56.120
And my spells usually have
a time limit to them.

14:56.120 --> 14:58.250
A temporary spell would be fine, too.

14:58.250 --> 15:03.170
The thing is, my grandmother said that
she'll be testing me on the tea ceremony.

15:03.630 --> 15:06.840
And if I don't pass,
my lessons will increase.

15:07.260 --> 15:11.180
I don't want my adolescence
to be stolen by these lessons anymore.

15:12.930 --> 15:15.510
Having your life filled with lessons is tough.

15:15.510 --> 15:17.140
A tea ceremony, huh?

15:17.140 --> 15:19.560
Lots of purposeful,
careful movements are involved.

15:19.810 --> 15:22.440
I don't have any spells
that make you skillful, but...

15:22.440 --> 15:24.360
Moi, can I see your hand?

15:25.020 --> 15:26.360
You, too, Kiyomiya.

15:27.030 --> 15:28.110
Here you go.

15:32.570 --> 15:34.450
Synclone!

15:37.370 --> 15:39.210
Now Moi, try moving your hand.

15:43.000 --> 15:44.590
She's moving just like me.

15:45.040 --> 15:48.170
On the day of the test, I'll cast
this spell on your bodies, and Moi

15:48.170 --> 15:51.340
can control your movements from
a different room. Let's go with that strategy.

15:51.590 --> 15:54.140
I have to master the tea ceremony now?

15:55.100 --> 15:56.970
<i>With that said...</i>

15:57.560 --> 15:59.480
<i>by independently
studying books and videos,</i>

15:59.640 --> 16:03.100
<i>and with help from the Tea Ceremony Club,
he actually mastered it!</i>

16:03.100 --> 16:05.230
I'm always so amazed.

16:08.070 --> 16:10.490
<i>Saturday, the Kiyomiya residence.</i>

16:10.900 --> 16:13.990
The test is tomorrow,
but let's practice today.

16:13.990 --> 16:16.490
The substitute test taker
is taking this seriously, huh?

16:16.660 --> 16:18.830
Wait, why are you here?

16:18.830 --> 16:21.500
We need Magami's help this time, too.

16:21.500 --> 16:23.750
I brought the gadget we talked about.

16:24.460 --> 16:27.000
There's a small camera
inside these glasses.

16:27.290 --> 16:29.000
You can feed the video to your smartphone.

16:29.170 --> 16:32.420
That way, we'll be able to see
what's going on in the tea room.

16:32.420 --> 16:34.510
Okay, since we have this room
to ourselves...

16:36.220 --> 16:38.760
We'll use duct tape to place
where everything is in the tea room.

16:41.730 --> 16:44.810
Kiyomiya, let's start rehearsing.

16:45.480 --> 16:47.310
Terrible news, everyone.

16:47.520 --> 16:50.280
Grandmother changed her schedule,
and is actually here today.

16:50.440 --> 16:52.610
And she wants to conduct the test
today as well.

16:52.610 --> 16:53.400
What?

16:58.490 --> 17:00.410
<i>It's suddenly test time, huh?</i>

17:00.660 --> 17:04.120
Listen well, Suzuka.
You understand, don't you?

17:04.370 --> 17:07.040
If you cannot pass a simple test like this,

17:07.040 --> 17:10.340
it's considered an embarrassment
as the daughter of the Kiyomiya family.

17:12.760 --> 17:14.470
Moi, you have to answer.

17:14.470 --> 17:15.800
Our mouths are synchronized, too?

17:15.930 --> 17:17.890
Our mouths are synchronized, too?

17:19.930 --> 17:20.720
<i>Suzuka?</i>

17:20.720 --> 17:24.020
Watch what you're saying!
Just say, "Yes, Grandmother."

17:24.020 --> 17:25.440
Yes, Grandmother.

17:25.940 --> 17:28.940
<i>This is really tough without a rehearsal.</i>

17:29.110 --> 17:31.280
You really are such a careless girl.

17:31.280 --> 17:35.070
Back in my day,
things were so very strict.

17:35.070 --> 17:36.570
Yes, Grandmother.

17:36.860 --> 17:41.950
However, you will come to appreciate
mastering such lessons in your later years.

17:41.950 --> 17:43.580
Yes, Grandmother.

17:43.750 --> 17:48.380
When you're an adult, you'll find that
etiquette keeps society running smoothly.

17:48.380 --> 17:49.840
Yes, Grandmother.

17:50.840 --> 17:53.170
Am I boring you?

17:53.170 --> 17:54.800
Yes, Grandmother.

17:55.510 --> 17:57.970
You have to pay attention
to what she's saying, Moi.

17:58.260 --> 18:01.720
Let's start from
when you enter the room. Begin!

18:04.480 --> 18:05.980
OPEN THE DOOR

18:06.270 --> 18:08.480
<i>There are three steps
when opening the door.</i>

18:08.900 --> 18:11.860
<i>Place your hand on the handle,
and slightly open it.</i>

18:12.360 --> 18:15.780
<i>Then, open the door half way with your hand
around 24 cm from the bottom.</i>

18:15.780 --> 18:19.740
<i>Switch to the opposite hand, and open
almost all the way, but not completely.</i>

18:20.240 --> 18:21.490
<i>Place your hand on the handle.</i>

18:24.660 --> 18:27.250
<i>Hand... on the handle...</i>

18:30.130 --> 18:31.630
<i>Is that a cat?</i>

18:35.090 --> 18:37.380
S-Suzuka?

18:37.800 --> 18:43.310
What's wrong? Won't you come in?
I'm getting a little scared.

18:44.850 --> 18:46.770
<i>I opened it in one fell swoop.</i>

18:47.140 --> 18:49.140
<i>You can do it, Otogi.</i>

18:49.140 --> 18:50.650
ENTER THE ROOM

18:50.940 --> 18:54.400
<i>When you enter, while still sitting
on your knees, you shuffle in slowly.</i>

18:54.940 --> 18:57.280
<i>First, place your sensu fan in front of you.</i>

18:57.820 --> 19:03.200
<i>Put both of your fists on the tatami,
lift yourself, and move forward.</i>

19:10.620 --> 19:13.170
It looks like she became
some kind of frog toy.

19:13.170 --> 19:16.920
Morihito's exerting the amount of strength
needed to move his own heavier body,

19:16.920 --> 19:20.090
but that amount of power is too much
for Kiyomiya's lighter body.

19:20.090 --> 19:23.220
I guess this spell doesn't take
those kinds of details into consideration.

19:25.720 --> 19:26.970
<i>Stare.</i>

19:28.480 --> 19:29.980
PARTAKE IN THE CANDY

19:30.390 --> 19:32.060
<i>Bow to the person next to you.</i>

19:32.440 --> 19:34.480
<i>Humbly accept the plate.</i>

19:35.360 --> 19:37.530
<i>Take out the folded paper
from your kimono.</i>

19:38.190 --> 19:42.620
<i>Unfold it with the creases towards you,
set it down, and place the candy atop it.</i>

19:43.370 --> 19:45.870
Dang, Morihito really mastered this, huh?

19:45.870 --> 19:47.830
They put out some rakugan candy.

19:48.250 --> 19:50.000
We'll use Country Ma'am cookies
as a replacement.

19:58.710 --> 19:59.760
<i>Too fast!</i>

20:01.130 --> 20:03.390
A-Are you all right, Suzuka?

20:03.550 --> 20:05.300
I think she might be choking.

20:05.300 --> 20:09.890
You can't eat a Country Ma'am cookie
at the same pace of a dry candy.

20:09.890 --> 20:12.770
<i>But that's what I was given,
so it can't be helped!</i>

20:15.110 --> 20:17.020
What is it, Suzuka?
Are you in your rebellious age?

20:17.020 --> 20:18.530
PARTAKE IN THE TEA

20:18.780 --> 20:20.780
I humbly thank you for the tea.

20:21.200 --> 20:23.280
<i>Pick up the side of the bowl
with your right hand,</i>

20:23.820 --> 20:25.530
<i>and use your left hand
to hold the bottom.</i>

20:26.080 --> 20:29.790
<i>Turn the bowl twice in the clockwise direction
as you avoid the front of the bowl.</i>

20:30.200 --> 20:33.170
<i>I can't see the position of her mouth
to the bowl, so just drink with instinct!</i>

20:38.880 --> 20:40.920
Thank you for the delicious tea.

20:41.050 --> 20:42.420
It's all over you!

20:42.420 --> 20:43.680
WIPE THE BOWL WITH YOUR FINGER

20:45.470 --> 20:47.930
Please do wipe your mouth!

20:47.930 --> 20:49.180
ADMIRE THE BOWL

20:49.520 --> 20:53.940
Now isn't the time for admiration!
You look just like Kinnikuman!

20:54.900 --> 20:56.650
You do not pass!

20:58.570 --> 21:03.450
Suzuka, you fail to understand
the meaning behind learning these lessons.

21:03.570 --> 21:06.410
The performing arts and martial arts
have meaning behind every movement.

21:06.410 --> 21:07.660
Not a single movement is wasted.

21:07.660 --> 21:11.620
And so, at the root of these beautiful movements
is where you find a person's heart.

21:12.910 --> 21:15.080
You will learn everything again
from the beginning.

21:15.790 --> 21:16.500
A bee!

21:16.500 --> 21:18.340
It's not "Yee," it's "Yes"!

21:18.420 --> 21:19.460
It's a giant hornet!

21:22.210 --> 21:26.640
Oh, no, a bee! I hate them so much!

21:26.640 --> 21:27.720
<i>Grandmother!</i>

21:28.050 --> 21:29.220
<i>I have to go help them.</i>

21:29.850 --> 21:30.720
No.

21:33.310 --> 21:35.060
Ogre Qigong Fighting Style...

21:37.730 --> 21:38.980
FIREFLY TRAP

21:38.060 --> 21:38.980
Firefly Trap!

21:54.210 --> 21:56.250
<i>It was in this moment
that Setsuko Kiyomiya...</i>

21:56.670 --> 22:00.340
<i>would later proclaim that she saw the most
beautiful performance she had ever seen.</i>

22:01.460 --> 22:02.760
And so,

22:03.170 --> 22:07.590
after saving Grandmother from that bee,
and completing the ceremony,

22:07.800 --> 22:13.350
she judged that I may still have hope,
and withdrew the failure.

22:13.350 --> 22:15.480
Oh, that's great news.

22:15.480 --> 22:16.520
Also...

22:16.520 --> 22:19.480
for next time, I was told that
it sounds like the devil's temari song,

22:19.690 --> 22:22.320
but I have a test in koto coming up.

22:22.980 --> 22:25.320
Otogi, would you like to master
the koto next?

22:25.320 --> 22:26.990
No thank you!

23:57.450 --> 23:59.620
All right, did you enjoy that video?

23:59.620 --> 24:03.130
If you thought it was funny, please click on that
"like" button and also subscribe!

24:03.130 --> 24:03.920
Ready, and...

24:03.920 --> 24:06.590
The sun Kan shine, let's smile with Nico.
Chan-bala daba daba, dance the Lambada.

24:06.590 --> 24:09.720
Dai dara bocchi, witch watcchi. Go, go, go!
And then clap your hands, clap, clap!

24:06.590 --> 24:11.970
NEXT EPISODE
KANSHI'S PART-TIME JOB DIARIES
~THE SUPERHERO SHOW~
KANSHI'S PART-TIME JOB DIARIES
~THE SIDE JOB~

24:09.720 --> 24:11.970
Look right, look left, and head bang king!
